    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d169">

                <pb facs="0458" n="423" sameAs="frus:frus1977-80v29/pg423"/>

                <head>169. Memorandum From Acting Secretary of State Christopher to President
                        Carter<anchor n="1" xml:id="d169-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1978-04-20">April 20, 1978</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>[Omitted here is information unrelated to Panama.]</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Panama Canal Treaties</hi>. With the ratification of the
                    Treaties behind us, we will be following up in a number of areas. Attached is a
                    memorandum outlining next steps.</p>


                <xi:include href="d169-a1.xml" xpointer="d169-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d169-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d169-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Carter Library, National Security Affairs, Brzezinski Material, Subject
                    File, Box 20, Evening Reports (State), 4/78. Secret. Carter initialed the
                    memorandum and wrote: “Warren.” Vance was in Moscow meeting with General
                    Secretary Brezhnev.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
